## Why This Is Asked
This question tests advanced AWS authorization patterns including ABAC with IAM tags, Lake Formation permissions, and cross-account data governance in regulated environments. It probes understanding of data catalog discipline, encryption strategies, revocation latency requirements, and external auditor access workflows.

## Key Concepts
- IAM tag-based access control (TBAC) combined with Lake Formation fine-grained grants
- Cross-account role trusts with least-privilege permission boundaries
- S3 prefix-level isolation per tenant with envelope encryption (KMS)
- Data catalog resource links and table/column-level permissions
- Audit trail generation via Athena, CloudTrail, and Lake Formation audit logs

## Solution Architecture

### Cross-Account Trust Model
```javascript
// Analytics Account Trust Policy (tenant-specific role)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Principal": {
      "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::INGEST_ACCOUNT:root"
    },
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
    "Condition": {
      "StringEquals": {
        "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${s3:tenant-id}"
      },
      "StringLike": {
        "s3:prefix": "data-lake/${s3:tenant-id}/*"
      }
    }
  }]
}
```

### IAM Tag-Based Permission Policy
```javascript
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Action": [
      "s3:GetObject",
      "s3:PutObject",
      "s3:ListBucket"
    ],
    "Resource": [
      "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake",
      "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*"
    ],
    "Condition": {
      "StringEquals": {
        "s3:prefix": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*"
      }
    }
  }]
}
```

### Lake Formation Grant Scope
- Grant DATABASE permission on tenant-specific catalog databases
- Grant TABLE permission filtered to tenant-prefixed table patterns
- Use data catalog resource links in Analytics account pointing to Governance catalog

## Test Plan

| Test Case | Expected Result |
|-----------|-----------------|
| Tenant A reads own data | Access granted via matched tag |
| Tenant A reads Tenant B data | Access denied—prefix mismatch |
| Revoke Tenant A access | Role trust removed within 2 hours via IAM/Lake Formation API |
| External auditor cross-account read | Time-limited read-only role with Athena query access |
| Audit log verification | CloudTrail shows principal, tenant-id, timestamp, resource |

## External Auditor Sharing
Grant time-limited read-only access via a dedicated auditor role in the Governance account with Athena query permissions restricted to specific databases.

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable, compliant multi-tenant real-time pipeline with data residency requirements, cross-account access, and disaster recovery.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation and per-tenant data locality
- Exactly-once delivery semantics across streaming and storage
- Cross-account IAM with STS and least privilege
- DR planning across regions, cost-aware choices
- Observability with CloudWatch, X-Ray

## Code Example
